   - **On/off toggle**: a switch in Security Center's Shield tab, backed by `user_settings.py`'s `shield_protection_enabled` (same settings.json every other preference already uses). `darkos-protect.py` checks it every ~30s via a `_reconcile` step and starts/stops the real watcher accordingly — takes effect within that window, not instantly, stated as the real trade-off it is rather than built to look instant and not be.
   - **Review/restore UI**: a Quarantine tab in Security Center, real entries, Restore/Delete-permanently wired to the real calls. Surfaced two more real bugs by actually rendering it: the same GTK3 stock-chrome gap on `Gtk.ListBox`/`row` that `scale`/`levelbar`/`progressbar` already had (fixed the same way), and an unellipsized path overflow that pushed the action buttons off the visible row (fixed, and now has a regression test specifically because it happened).
   - **Removable media (2026-09-11)**: `discover_mount_dirs()` checks `/run/media/$USER` and `/media/$USER` every ~30s (same cycle as the toggle); anything found gets added via `ContinuousWatcher.add_watch_path()`. Found a real foundational gap while scoping this: neither `udisks2` nor `gvfs` were in `packages.x86_64` at all, so removable media wasn't auto-mounting in the first place — added both, since watching a mount point nothing ever populates isn't real coverage. This surfaced a genuine, non-obvious testing pitfall too: `GLib.get_user_config_dir()` (what `user_settings.py`'s `settings_path()` calls) caches its result for the whole process after the first call, so patching `$HOME` mid-test doesn't work reliably — cost real debugging time to track down, now documented in the test file itself and fixed by patching `settings_path` directly instead, in all three places that needed it.
